@host = http://localhost:5192

### The OpenAPI document: each operation documents the success status code it's sent with.
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

### The same document as a ReDoc page (open it in a browser).
GET {{host}}/api-docs/v1/

### 200, a GET keeps the default: the list and its items.
GET {{host}}/api/lists/1

### 404, Hlibz.Results' ErrorResponse.
GET {{host}}/api/lists/99

### 201 Created, Location: /api/lists/2 (WithCreatedLocation).
POST {{host}}/api/lists
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Chores" }

### 400, validation errors: a blank title, the rule the document's "x-rules" states.
POST {{host}}/api/lists
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "  " }

### 201 Created, Location: /api/lists/1/items/2 (WithCreatedLocation).
POST {{host}}/api/lists/1/items
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Bread" }

### 200, a POST that creates nothing keeps the default: the item, now done.
POST {{host}}/api/lists/1/items/1/complete

### 409, the item is already done.
POST {{host}}/api/lists/1/items/1/complete

### 204 No Content, the app-wide default for DELETE.
DELETE {{host}}/api/lists/1/items/1

### 204 No Content, the list is gone.
DELETE {{host}}/api/lists/2

### 404, a failure keeps its own status, whatever the success code.
DELETE {{host}}/api/lists/99
